     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Thinking that a longer arm means a bigger angle: the **opening** matters, not the length of the lines.\n- Calling 120° acute: it is more than 90°, so it is **obtuse**.\n- Forgetting that a straight line is also an angle (180°)."
    },
